Falsifies `memory_region_heap::verification::the_bytes_a_grow_asks_for_never_overflow`.

The defect: the alignment slack is doubled, "to be safe", so an over-aligned request adds twice its
alignment to the chunk. A valid layout may carry an alignment of 2^63, and twice that does not fit
in a `usize`.

Expected to fail: an overflow check on the multiplication. Red in under a second on 2026-11-15.

diff --git a/crates/memory_region_heap/src/growth.rs b/crates/memory_region_heap/src/growth.rs
index 21337a449..f620f0b5a 100644
--- a/crates/memory_region_heap/src/growth.rs
+++ b/crates/memory_region_heap/src/growth.rs
@@ -62,7 +62,7 @@ pub(crate) fn required_bytes(
 ) -> u64 {
     let chunk = (layout.size() + core::mem::size_of::<usize>()).next_multiple_of(chunk_unit);
     let over_aligned = if layout.align() > chunk_unit {
-        layout.align()
+        layout.align() * 2
     } else {
         0
     };
